There's no attempt to fake scsi in the atapi driver (which would require to
emulate some commands, and would be a lot of work which desn't need to be
in the kernel). It's just the interface for sending commands which is the
same. In general scsi commands will work with atapi devices too but 
if something is different between scsi and atapi the program has to take
care of that.

